          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"photon-vacuum-polarization\">Photon vacuum polarization</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Generate the electron loop and reduce its numerator in <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(D=4-2\\epsilon||)</marimo-tex>.\nThe result is transverse: <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||((p^2g^{\\mu\\nu}-p^\\mu p^\\nu)F(p^2)||)</marimo-tex>.\nKeeping <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(D||)</marimo-tex> symbolic until after reduction retains the finite rational term.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The scalar masters use the shared OneLOop evaluator. The expressions below\nomit the common loop factor <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(i/(16\\pi^2)||)</marimo-tex>; the UV coefficient is\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(-4e^2/3||)</marimo-tex>. Numerical values use <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(e=m^2=\\mu^2=1||)</marimo-tex> and show the physical\nimaginary part above the pair-production threshold <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(p^2=4m^2||)</marimo-tex>.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
